EXT. SHELLED FARMHOUSE - DAWN

Smoke. Rubble. A dead cow. Ahead, a treeline hums with distant engines.

SGT. BRANDT, 40s, crouches behind a half-wall, rifle across his knees. LT. ACHTERBERG, 30s, studies a map, mud on his glasses. A YOUNG SOLDIER, 19, trembles beside them, helmet too big.

BRANDT
(to everyone)
Heads down. Listen.

The engines swell. The Young Soldier lifts his head.

BRANDT (CONT'D)
Down!

Achterberg folds the map.

ACHTERBERG
Armor. Two, maybe three.

BRANDT
Our guns?

ACHTERBERG
Dead.

YOUNG SOLDIER
(to himself)
Mama. Mama. Mama.

BRANDT
What's your name, son?

YOUNG SOLDIER
Kowalski.

BRANDT
Kowalski. Look at me. On my word, you run for the ditch. You don't stop.

KOWALSKI
Sergeant, I can't --

BRANDT
You can.

A shell lands close. Dirt rains on all three of them.

ACHTERBERG
(to Brandt)
Now?

BRANDT
Now!
